## Review boundaries

The evaluation display is a static explanation, not execution or a debugger. Optional chains, assignments, increment/decrement, delete and typeof expressions stay whole until their distinct evaluation semantics can be shown accurately. No breakpoint control is advertised without a debugger. Human acceptance remains pending, and the subsequent execution-system stage remains gated on that review.
